															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nicknirus" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3061946); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3061946&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606596000" alt="NickNirus" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3061946)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nicknirus" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3061946); return false;" >NickNirus</a></span> <span class="odate time_1509642514 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 Nov 2017 17:08</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3624853">
									

<p>This made me so hype I legit needed a minute to collect my thoughts. I'm a sucker for computer SCPs in general, but they don't normally give me goosebumps. This one did.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">!sreliopS</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I really like the AI's personality, it feels a couple steps removed from a normal human being, which is a great way to do an AI. The portrayal of an adversarial neural net as siblings fighting is just beautiful, and the final twist made me want to re-read the article to get all the hints.</p>
<p>The one thing I didn't catch at all is the necromancy, although it was rather clear when you pointed it out. I would suggest showing that the people who were saved by the AI remain connected to it somehow, like mentioning that the app can be deleted, but nobody ever does that.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>The way you talk about cryptocurrencies is a nice touch. I like the idea that even for something that anti-authoritarian and decentralised, the Foundation can just go &quot;yeah, just make a bubble, pop it in ██ years, sweep the remains in a box and put in on a shelf&quot;.</p>
<p>Overall, a great article and a definite +1!</p>

							</div>

								
					
